- Run in Sapam, Vietnam; drawing based on a dense bamboo forest encounter.
- Clusters of roughly 20-30 bamboo trees packed close together.
- Dark, cool forest feel, especially at night or early morning.
- Steep hill near the finish of a 100-kilometer run.
- Dense trees created disorientation; felt like the whole earth was that hill.
- Slower, deliberate pace that felt like rest.
- Pause for reflection and observation within the stillness.
- Desire to appreciate and cherish the rare, different moment.
- Drawing made a few weeks after the run.
